one of the great things about the  bitcoin network is that on-chain  analytics allows us to see the flow of  funds that includes having identified  all of the wallets for the large  exchanges we can see how much are going  on to exchanges and how much bitcoin is  being taken off of the exchanges  watching to see when bitcoin comes off  exchanges is really important that means  the market's getting more illiquid you  can't just sit there and press a button  on an exchange and sell bitcoin if the  bitcoin's not there and it's been taken  off into cold storage and so watching  this metric is a key component of  understanding where price may go moving  forward well if we go ahead and we take  a look for the first time in a couple of  months binance one of the world's  largest exchanges is now showing that  bitcoin is coming off there's net  outflows on binance why is binance  specifically so important well if we go  ahead and we take a look at the charts  what we can see is that the overall  exchange balances of bitcoin has been  coming down since september of last year  but binance had actually been increasing  so binance was bucking the trend they  were going up in their bitcoin on the  exchange while all other exchanges were  coming down if we then go ahead and we  take a look now binance is having net  outflows as well and so if we go ahead  and we take a look we can see that on  all exchanges the bitcoin balance is  drastically coming down including on  binance you can see it right there  circled at the bottom right of this  chart and so now that we have binance  outflows then we can go ahead and  extrapolate this out what is going on on  the macro basis of all exchanges you can  see here with this orange line that the  balance on exchanges has been coming  down since about the end of 2019  actually and that coincides with a  massive run-up in price if we then go  ahead and we zoom in on january of 2020  what we can see is that january 2020  until now balances on exchanges is just  an absolute freefall this shows that the  bitcoin market is becoming more illiquid  it's becoming much easier for new demand  to push the price up and what we've seen  over that time period is that bitcoin  went from about 8 000 or so all the way  up to 69 000 today sits around 40 000  and so then if we can see over time the  inflows and outflows of these exchange  balances you can see that it hasn't  always been pure net outflows in the  green you see there are times of inflows  but right now over the last couple of  months since about the beginning of 2022  pretty much everyone is taking bitcoin  off of exchanges they're not putting it  on that is usually a sign that in the  future bitcoin's price will increase you  have an illiquid market you have  increasing demand price has to move to  accommodate everyone there is no way to  actually predict the future but on chain  metrics show you what's already  occurring and it's a great signal of  what could be to come continue to pay  attention to this exact metric of the  balances for exchanges because what it's  likely to show how illiquid the market  is and that is one of the key components  to understanding future bitcoin price  movements hey you did you like this  video great we make five of them a day  and post them here on this channel make  sure you subscribe like the video and  see you next time
 

